== Order Statistics & Matrix Dot Products
- The sample minimum $min(x)$ slightly overestimates $a$ and $max(x)$ slightly underestimates $b$; the linear combination stretches them by $frac(1, n-1)(max(x) - min(x))$.
- Matrix multiplication takes the dot product of row $i$ of $A$ with column $j$ of $B$.
